@kind(writ)

#[ Writ: pure-unused-allow fixture ]

##[ parser-purity ]

@rule(parser-purity){
  guard: { twrit: pure }

  pure: {
    crates: [ "core" ]
    forbid: [ ]
    allow-external: [ "outside", "gone" ]
  }
}

`core` reaches `outside`, which is listed. `gone` is listed and reached by
nothing: an entry that outlived the dependency it was written for.

An allowlist is worth more than "no external dependencies" because it says
what is true. A dead entry makes it say something that is not.
